{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nProf. Vasechkin wants to represent positive integer n as a sum of addends, where each addends is an integer number containing only 1s. For example, he can represent 121 as 121=111+11+\u20131. Help him to find the least number of digits 1 in such sum.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n  static final long[] R = {0, 1, 11, 111, 1111, 11111, 111111, 1111111, 11111111, 111111111, 1111111111L, 11111111111L, 111111111111L, 1111111111111L, 11111111111111L, 111111111111111L};\n\n  static class FastReader {\n    InputStream in;\n    BufferedReader br;\n    StringTokenizer st;\n\n    FastReader(InputStream i) {\n      in = i;\n      br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(i));\n    }\n\n    String next() throws IOException {\n      while (st == null || !st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n        st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n      }\n      return st.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    long nextLong() throws IOException {\n      return Long.parseLong(next());\n    }\n  }\n\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    FastReader fr = new FastReader(System.in);\n    long n = fr.nextLong();\n    System.out.println(f(n));\n  }\n\n  static long f(long x) {\n    if (x <= 6) return x;\n    int len = Long.toString(x).length();\n    long rep = R[len];\n    if (x == rep) return len;\n    long prev = R[len - 1];\n    long next = R[len + 1];\n    long cost1 = (x / rep) * len + f(x % rep);\n    long cost2 = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n    if (next - x <= x) {\n      cost2 = f(next - x) + (len + 1);\n    }\n    return Math.min(cost1, cost2);\n  }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n  static final long[] R = {0, 1, 11, 111, 1111, 11111, 111111, 1111111, 11111111, 111111111, 1111111111L, 11111111111L, 111111111111L, 1111111111111L, 11111111111111L, 111111111111111L, 1111111111111111L, 11111111111111111L, 111111111111111111L, 1111111111111111111L};\n\n  static class FastReader {\n    InputStream in;\n    BufferedReader br;\n    StringTokenizer st;\n\n    FastReader(InputStream i) {\n      in = i;\n      br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(i));\n    }\n\n    String next() throws IOException {\n      while (st == null || !st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n        st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n      }\n      return st.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    long nextLong() throws IOException {\n      return Long.parseLong(next());\n    }\n  }\n\n  static long[] memo = new long[100000];\n\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n    FastReader fr = new FastReader(System.in);\n    long n = fr.nextLong();\n    System.out.println(f(n));\n  }\n\n  static long f(long x) {\n    if (x <= 0) return 0;\n    if (x < memo.length) {\n      if (memo[(int)x] != 0) return memo[(int)x];\n    }\n    \n    if (x <= 6) {\n      if (x < memo.length) memo[(i